MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 91ed8fbac4f95a646a385ee421129d7d, type: 3}
  m_Name: GateOfEmotions_EN
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  introductionText: You are about to enter a different state of awareness...
  selectTwoEmotionsText: Which emotions do you feel more frequently? Choose 2.
  anger: Anger
  fear: Fear
  joy: Joy
  sadness: Sadness
  question1: How pleasant or unpleasant do you feel?
  question2: How high or low is your energy?
  question3: What would you call this feeling?
  pleasant: Pleasant
  unpleasant: Unpleasant
  highEnergy: Energetic
  lowEnergy: Low energy
  feedbackAnger: Anger is triggered when someone hurts us in some way, because it
    crosses the boundaries of some value, such as respect, care or justice.... It
    fills you with energy because you need it to protect something valuable to you.
  feedbackFear: 'Fear is triggered when we perceive that something valuable is in
    danger. It paralyzes you so that you can assess that danger, and makes you want
    to flee or run away to protect yourself from it. '
  feedbackJoy: Joy is triggered when we achieve something valuable. It is like an
    emotional reward, it fills you with vitality and optimism so you can go on with
    your plans and keep doing important things.
  feedbackSadness: 'Sadness is triggered when we suffer the loss of something valuable.
    It can be overwhelming... But it has a function: it drains you of energy so you
    can stop, cry, grieve, remember, reflect... and pull yourself together.'
  feedbackIncorrect: "This doesn\u2019t seem to be the emotion that you are feeling
    right now, try again\u2026"
